🇺🇸 Seeing Past the Daily Political Circus in Washington... 

▪️Washington is a layer of interface between the actual corporate interests that run the US, and the American/global public;

▪️The political circus performed by Washington daily is designed to keep people divided (both between "left/right" but also within parties) and distracted, as well as invested in the political circus preventing real awareness/mobilization from taking place;

▪️Those performing this daily political circus including Tulsi Gabbard and JD Vance seek to keep you invested in your political party of choice despite consistent betrayal by that party;

▪️Much of this is compartmentalization (for example: "Trump and others in his administration turned out to be rotten liars, but JD Vance! He's still on point!") is designed to keep you locked in despite the demonstrated futility of Western electoral politics:

▪️There are also limited hangouts like Joe Kent pushing the "Israel made us do it" which contradicts the "JD Vance is putting Israel in its place," - as long as these performances are things people want to see and believe, they'll buy it no matter how unrealistic, contradictory, or detached from reality all of it is;

▪️this is how people are kept locked into this cycle of "elect and regret" and constant cycles of hope/betrayal;

▪️If people don't look past this political circus, they will never see the interests behind it and benefiting from it - if they can't see reality in the first place, there is no way to come up with solutions to improve it - and the cycle will continue as designed;
